# Reference lab (.github/workflows/reference-lab.yml): what a push runs.
# The plan and its rules: BACKLOG §0 "Reference lab"; skill ui-design §4
# (MX is a reference for proportions and behaviour, never for looks).
#
# 22 Nov 2026: fetch the MX Player the owner has on the phone (installed
# from the Play Store, version 3.4.3, read off the phone's App info) and keep
# it in the private repository innocent-ref. Nothing to compare with yet.
#   run 44984807250: innocent-ref reached (private); listed Google Play,
#     apkeep 1.1.0's default source, not APKPure.
#   run 44985066077: APKPure lists 63 versions (1.85.8 to 3.5.3), 3.4.3
#     among them; no x86_64 build of it. Run 3: arm64-v8a, x86_64 optional.
#   run 44985566401: 3.4.3 arm64-v8a and 1.85.8 downloaded; the base APK did
#     not verify (apksigner). Run 4 prints apksigner's reason.
# Next: MODE=probe (does it run on the lab's emulator).
MODE=fetch
MX_PACKAGE=com.mxtech.videoplayer.ad
MX_VERSION=3.4.3
# The signer's SHA-256 (or SHA-1) from a second source, when one is read;
# APKMirror was not reachable from the session on 22 Nov.
MX_CERT=
